From 77883aad7356135ebca1a32ba2fde5ecb186966c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:32:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] r4.1 world flow: backgrounding mid-exit / mid-walk-home
 freezes the walk and continues it on return (no snap to the chair, no exit
 replay); exit track resumes at its offset
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Grok Bot (evidence voice-bot 20261017T121502Z-r4-exit-footsteps/recording-yunjing/C_gating/C_show_snapback_strip.png):
hidden halfway through the exit, she came back on the chair and replayed the whole exit; BGM "restarted".

Root cause (WorldFlowCore V1 83de245): hide() invalidate()d the running leaveHome (token + all jobs cancelled),
restore()d the stable pose (stable is still 'home' until the exit ends = seated, home camera) and changed to 'paused';
show() then called leaveHome() again from the seat. The walk home had the same cancel: she was put back on the island
behind 「继续」. Audio: the replay re-entered 'standing' (GameAudio quietAmbience hard-stops wind/waves, exit track
cancel:restart) and played sfx_exit_outbound again from 0 at the replayed doorway. The BGM loop itself was paused and
resumed in place (cross-correlation of the C_gating recording against bgm_main: offset before hide = t+1.228 s, after
show = t-2.788 s, i.e. exactly the 4.02 s hidden); what sounded like a restart was the replayed exit track and beds.

Fix:
- WorldFlowCore: hide() during an EXIT_STATES or new RETURN_STATES walk (walking-home, crossing-in, closing-door,
  walking-to-seat, sitting) freezes it: no invalidate, no restore, state kept, hidden+needsResume stop both clocks
  (advance() and WorldFlowComponent.update's job loop), so position, clip time, camera progress, door, light ramps and
  wind hold. show() lifts the freeze by itself (no 继续) and the same promise continues. V1's restart-from-seat removed.
  invalidate()/cancelTransition/fault drop a freeze. Seated / island / level / journey / sky visit unchanged.
- WorldFlowComponent: after a show that resumed by itself, re-apply the ambient / room-light host pause from the layers
  on screen (onHide paused them; setLayers is not called on this path).
- GameAudio: a background trip during 'crossing-out' holds the exit track's segment offset; when audio is back it
  continues at that offset (one voice, no maxLateS drop, nothing past the clip end). Interruption and the island tail
  keep the old rule; any world state change drops the hold. sfxMuted gates still 3.
- Footsteps (cfe6429): the frozen motion clock does not move, the flow state never changes across the trip, so the
  tracker neither resets nor fires a plant twice.

Test world-background-freeze (run-suite): every exit / walk-home state x hidden 3 s / 10 s x with/without frames while
hidden: position, clip time, camera, door, wind, jobs identical before/while/after; no paused/home/standing re-entry, no
cancelAndReset, no second leaveHome/load; same state sequence and active time as an uninterrupted run; seated/island/
cancel unchanged; GameAudio on a Cocos-3.8.8-semantics AudioSource mock: BGM paused not stopped, same offset, no
restart; exit track continues at its offset with one voice; footsteps same plants as uninterrupted, none doubled.
test-exit-background-resume: comments updated (exit now continues instead of restarting); assertions unchanged.
